        "question": {
          ":question/id": "b1feca3f-c0c4-5a2c-85a6-124153de18c9",
          ":question/problem": "Find $f_x(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=\\tan{\\left(\\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 y + 2 \\right)} \\right)}$.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Treat $y$ as constant and differentiate with respect to $x$. Apply the chain rule, and the sum and constant multiple rules where needed.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=3 x + 2 y + 2\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}&=3\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\tan(\\ln u)&=\\sec^2(\\ln u)\\cdot\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}\\\\\nf_x(x,y)&=\\left(\\frac{\\sec^{2}{\\left(\\ln{\\left(u \\right)} \\right)}}{u}\\right)\\cdot\\left(3\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{3 \\sec^{2}{\\left(\\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 y + 2 \\right)} \\right)}}{3 x + 2 y + 2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThese derivatives apply for $3 x + 2 y + 2>0$ and $\\cos(\\ln(3 x + 2 y + 2))\\ne0$.",
