        "question": {
          ":question/id": "da2e32d7-e21f-5d86-b0a9-3fa203267b9e",
          ":question/problem": "For the function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=2 x^{2} y + \\ln{\\left(e^{- 2 x^{2} + y} + 1 \\right)},\n$$\n\nevaluate both partial derivatives at $(-1,-2)$.\n\n$f_x(-1,-2)=$\n\n{{field-1}}\n\n$f_y(-1,-2)=$\n\n{{field-2}}",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Treat $y$ as constant and differentiate with respect to $x$. Apply the chain rule, and the sum and constant multiple rules where needed.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=- 2 x^{2} + y\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}&=- 4 x\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\ln(1+e^u)&=\\frac{1}{1+e^u}\\cdot e^u\\cdot\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(2 x^{2} y\\right)&=4 x y\\\\\nf_x(x,y)&=\\left(\\frac{e^{u}}{e^{u} + 1}\\right)\\cdot\\left(- 4 x\\right)+\\left(4 x y\\right)\\\\\n&=4 x y - \\frac{4 x e^{- 2 x^{2} + y}}{e^{- 2 x^{2} + y} + 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=-1$ and $y=-2$ after differentiating. The inner input is\n\n$$\nu_0=- 2 \\left(-1\\right)^{2} + \\left(-2\\right)=-4.\n$$\n\nUsing this value in the chain factors gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x(-1,-2)&=\\left(\\frac{e^{u_0}}{e^{u_0} + 1}\\right)\\cdot\\left(4\\right)+\\left(8\\right)\\\\\n&=\\left(\\frac{1}{\\left(e^{-4} + 1\\right) e^{4}}\\right)\\cdot\\left(4\\right)+\\left(8\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{4 \\left(3 + 2 e^{4}\\right)}{1 + e^{4}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTreat $x$ as constant and differentiate with respect to $y$. Apply the chain rule, and the sum and constant multiple rules where needed.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=- 2 x^{2} + y\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y}&=1\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\ln(1+e^u)&=\\frac{1}{1+e^u}\\cdot e^u\\cdot\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y}\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(2 x^{2} y\\right)&=2 x^{2}\\\\\nf_y(x,y)&=\\left(\\frac{e^{u}}{e^{u} + 1}\\right)\\cdot\\left(1\\right)+\\left(2 x^{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=2 x^{2} + \\frac{e^{- 2 x^{2} + y}}{e^{- 2 x^{2} + y} + 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=-1$ and $y=-2$ after differentiating. The inner input is\n\n$$\nu_0=- 2 \\left(-1\\right)^{2} + \\left(-2\\right)=-4.\n$$\n\nUsing this value in the chain factors gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_y(-1,-2)&=\\left(\\frac{e^{u_0}}{e^{u_0} + 1}\\right)\\cdot\\left(1\\right)+\\left(2\\right)\\\\\n&=\\left(\\frac{1}{\\left(e^{-4} + 1\\right) e^{4}}\\right)\\cdot\\left(1\\right)+\\left(2\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{3 + 2 e^{4}}{1 + e^{4}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThese derivatives apply for all real $x,y$.",
